1. SCOPE, OWNERSHIP AND RESERVATION OF RIGHTS

The Cuelist's original source code, object code, project, interface, artwork
and documentation are proprietary copyrighted works, subject to applicable
law, including Italian Law No. 633 of 22 April 1941 on computer programs.

All rights not expressly granted are reserved to their respective lawful
owners. Public availability of the repository, files or revision history is
not an open-source licence, a waiver or permission for additional uses.
This licence applies only to original material lawfully controlled by the
relevant rights holders. It does not claim ownership of JUCE, third-party
components or independently licensed contributions.

2. VIEWING SOURCE CODE ON GITHUB

When the repository is public, GitHub's Terms of Service may permit viewing
and forking through GitHub's functionality, together with copies necessary
within the relevant platform permissions. Those rights are not an additional
licence to exploit, incorporate, sell or redistribute the software outside
the permitted scope.

Source availability alone does not authorize building and distributing
copies, republishing the code as one's own, developing products or services
from it, or replacing its proprietary licence with another licence.

3. PROHIBITED COPYING, MODIFICATION AND REUSE

Without the lawful rights holder's prior, explicit authorization, except
where mandatory law or applicable platform terms provide otherwise, it is
prohibited to:

(a) copy, publish, transmit, share or redistribute all or substantial
    portions of the original code, even without payment or under a new name;
(b) modify, translate, adapt, port, create derivatives of, or incorporate
    original code into other programs, products, services, repositories or
    libraries;
(c) build, package, market, sublicense, sell, rent or distribute unauthorized
    copies of the source or executable software;
(d) misrepresent authorship or remove or falsify ownership, copyright and
    attribution notices;
(e) purport to license the original source to third parties or relicense
    it under open-source or other terms without the rights holder's consent.

These restrictions apply to noncommercial uses too, subject to the stated
exceptions. This licence does not create an exclusive right in unprotected
ideas, principles or other noncopyrightable elements of software.

4. LAWFULLY ACQUIRED COPY: LICENCE TO USE

An authorized buyer or person with specific authorization obtains a
non-exclusive licence of indefinite duration to use the lawfully obtained
version for personal or professional purposes, under the supplied terms.

Unless otherwise agreed in writing, a commercial licence is purchased once
and allows installation on no more than two computers controlled by one
purchaser, without simultaneous use. There is no mandatory recurring
subscription to keep using the purchased version. Purchase does not transfer
copyright or grant the source-code permissions prohibited in Section 3.

Legally required operational and backup copies remain permitted. New major
versions may be priced separately, subject to mandatory updates, warranties
and remedies required by law and the sales offer.

5. ADDITIONAL PERMISSIONS AND MANDATORY RIGHTS

Further source-code reuse, modification or redistribution requires explicit
authorization from the lawful rights holder, defining scope and conditions.

Nothing here excludes non-waivable rights under applicable law, including
where applicable backup copies, studying how a program functions, and
interoperability under Articles 64-ter and 64-quater of Italian Law No. 633/1941,
consumer rights, lawful exhaustion or other statutory exceptions. No term
seeks to prohibit activities that applicable law does not permit to prohibit.

6. USER CONTENT AND THIRD-PARTY MATERIALS

User WAV/MP3, MIDI, show projects and other materials remain owned by their
respective rights holders. This licence does not grant permissions for
imported music, recordings or other works.

JUCE and other third-party components remain subject to their own licences
(see NOTICE.md and the relevant package's JUCE-LICENSE.md). These conditions
do not override those terms. A distributor must secure all necessary JUCE
rights separately; the existence of this document is not proof of them.

7. RELIABILITY, WARRANTIES AND SALES TERMS

The software may contain defects and must be tested with actual equipment
and emergency procedures before live use. All mandatory consumer rights,
statutory warranties and non-excludable liabilities remain unaffected.

Seller identity and contact details, pricing, delivery, withdrawal, support
and other required pre-contractual information are provided separately as
required by law. Authorized beta testing may be subject to additional
expressly communicated terms.

8. ENFORCEMENT

Unauthorized copying or distribution of original protected components may
infringe copyright and lead to remedies available under the law, regardless
of commercial gain or attribution. Absence of a notice in an individual file
does not waive copyright. The rights holder may consider appropriate
platform reporting and legal remedies.

This English translation is for convenience only. The Italian text controls.
